IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what my registered foundation must
-- do, and what can be done to me as one of its responsible persons: governance standards (ss 45-10(1), (5), (6)); records (s 55-5);
-- size (s 205-25); reporting (ss 60-5, 60-10, 60-20, 60-25, 60-60, 60-65, 60-85(2)(b)); the duty to notify (s 65-5); responsible
-- entity (s 205-30), federally regulated entity (s 205-15), basic religious charity (s 205-35); formal warnings (s 80-5);
-- suspension and removal of responsible entities (ss 100-5, 100-10, 100-15, 100-20, 100-25, 40-5(2)); administrative penalties for
-- false or misleading statements (ss 175-10, 175-20, 175-25, 175-30) and for lodging late (ss 175-35, 175-40); obligations,
-- liabilities and offences of trusts and their trustees' directors (ss 180-20, 180-25).
--
-- SEAT: the founder of a charity and director of its trustee company -- a responsible person of the registered entity (in
-- Daniel's life, the Rossi Foundation, a private ancillary fund; in 2076, his children as the new directors). "What must my
-- foundation do, and what can I be made to do or pay?" The Commissioner's beliefs and choices are asked as facts.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 11, compilation date 5 December 2025 (includes amendments up to Act No. 72, 2025), register id
-- C2025C00665, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2012A00168.txt. The Australian Charities and Not-for-profits
-- Commission Regulations 2022 are NOT DEPOSITED: the GOVERNANCE STANDARDS THEMSELVES ARE IN THEM, so compliance is an input and
-- their content is not encoded; any other size thresholds they prescribe under s 205-25(1), (2)(b) are inputs (the Act's own
-- figures are $250,000 and $1,000,000). The penalty unit is Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA ("$330 (subject to indexation under subsection
-- (3))"), Compilation No. 167, 27 August 2026, ../../../crimes-act-1914/registers/source-bundle/C1914A00012.txt -- an INPUT; s
-- 4B(3) of that Act (a body corporate may be fined up to 5 times the maximum for a natural person) is brought in for the records
-- offence. Revenue "in accordance with accounting standards" (s 205-25(4)) is a borrowed measure, asked as a fact.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The content of the governance standards and external conduct standards (Regulations, not deposited); financial
-- report contents (s 60-15, Regulations); auditor qualifications and reports (ss 60-30 to 60-55); additional reporting (ss 60-75,
-- 60-80); collective and joint reporting (ss 60-95 to 60-105); information gathering and monitoring (Divisions 70, 75); directions,
-- undertakings and injunctions (Divisions 85, 90, 95); acting responsible entities and vesting orders (Subdivisions 100-C, 100-D);
-- secrecy (Division 150); unincorporated associations and bodies corporate (Subdivisions 180-B, 180-D); the reduction of a base
-- penalty for following the Commissioner's advice (s 175-20(3)); remission (s 175-60); the general interest charge (s 175-65).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012 -- duties of registered entities and responsible persons`

§§ `s 205-30 -- am I a responsible entity`

-- s 205-30: "Each of the following is a responsible entity of a registered entity: (a) in the case of a registered entity that is a
-- company--a director of the registered entity; (b) in the case of a registered entity that is a trust--each of the following: (i)
-- a trustee of the registered entity; (ii) if a trustee of the registered entity is a body corporate--a director of the trustee; (c)
-- a person who is any of the following: (i) a trustee in bankruptcy ...; (ii) a receiver, or receiver and manager ...; (iii) an
-- administrator ...; (iv) an administrator of a deed of company arrangement ...; (v) a liquidator ...; (vi) a trustee or other entity
-- administering a compromise or arrangement". "director" (s 300-5): of an incorporated company, "a director of the company, or an
-- individual who performs the duties of a director ... regardless of the name that is given to his or her position, or whether or
-- not he or she is validly appointed". The governance standards are, by their nature, about the conduct of these persons; the Act
-- leaves their content to the Regulations (s 45-10).
DECLARE `My place in my foundation` HAS
    `my foundation is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my foundation is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a director of my foundation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a trustee of my foundation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a director of a body corporate that is its trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold an insolvency office in relation to it` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I a responsible entity (a responsible person) of my foundation (s 205-30)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My place in my foundation` @desc What your foundation is and the positions you hold; a director includes anyone who performs a director's duties, whatever the title or validity of appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a responsible entity` IF
        (`me`'s `my foundation is a company` AND `me`'s `I am a director of my foundation`)
    OR  (`me`'s `my foundation is a trust` AND (`me`'s `I am a trustee of my foundation` OR `me`'s `I am a director of a body corporate that is its trustee`))
    OR  `me`'s `I hold an insolvency office in relation to it`

§§ `s 205-15 -- is my foundation a federally regulated entity`

-- s 205-15: "A federally regulated entity is: (a) a constitutional corporation; or (b) a trust, all of the trustees of which are
-- constitutional corporations; or (c) a body corporate that is taken to be registered in a Territory under section 119A of the
-- Corporations Act 2001; or (d) a trust, if the proper law of the trust and the law of the trust's administration are the law of a
-- Territory; or (e) an entity, the core or routine activities of which are carried out in or in connection with a Territory." s
-- 205-20: a constitutional corporation is "(a) a corporation to which paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution applies; or (b) a body
-- corporate that is incorporated in a Territory" -- paragraph 51(xx) is borrowed, asked as a fact. Being one matters: the governance
-- standards are enforced by warning, suspension and removal only against a federally regulated entity (ss 80-5, 100-5).
DECLARE `What my foundation is` HAS
    `it is a constitutional corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a trust all of whose trustees are constitutional corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a body corporate taken to be registered in a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a trust whose proper law and law of administration are a Territory's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its core or routine activities are in or connected with a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my foundation a federally regulated entity (s 205-15)?
GIVEN `it` IS A `What my foundation is` @desc What kind of entity your foundation is and where it operates
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation a federally regulated entity` IF
        `it`'s `it is a constitutional corporation`
    OR  `it`'s `it is a trust all of whose trustees are constitutional corporations`
    OR  `it`'s `it is a body corporate taken to be registered in a Territory`
    OR  `it`'s `it is a trust whose proper law and law of administration are a Territory's`
    OR  `it`'s `its core or routine activities are in or connected with a Territory`

§§ `s 205-35 -- is my foundation a basic religious charity`

-- s 205-35(1): "(a) the entity is a registered entity; and (b) the entity is registered as the subtype ... (Entity with a purpose of
-- advancing religion); and (c) the entity is not entitled to be registered as any other subtype". (2): not if registered under the
-- Corporations Act 2001 or the CATSI Act, or incorporated under an associations incorporation Act. (3): "not ... if it is a
-- deductible gift recipient", subject to (3A) (a DGR only for funds under Subdivision 30-BA with revenue under $250,000 -- asked as a
-- fact). (4): not if in a reporting group. (5): not if government grants in the year or either of the previous 2 years exceed
-- $100,000. (6): not if named in an unwithdrawn National Redress Scheme application and not a participating institution -- asked as
-- a fact. A basic religious charity is outside the governance standards (s 45-10(5)), financial reporting (s 60-60) and suspension
-- and removal (s 100-5(3)).
DECLARE `My foundation's religious standing` HAS
    `it is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is registered only as advancing religion and entitled to no other subtype` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a Corporations Act or CATSI corporation or an incorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a deductible gift recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the s 205-35(3A) exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is in a reporting group` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the most government grants it received in this or either of the last 2 years` IS A NUMBER
    `it is named in a redress application and not a participating institution` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my foundation a basic religious charity (s 205-35)?
GIVEN `it` IS A `My foundation's religious standing` @desc How your foundation is registered, incorporated and funded
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation a basic religious charity` IF
        `it`'s `it is registered`
    AND `it`'s `it is registered only as advancing religion and entitled to no other subtype`
    AND (NOT `it`'s `it is a Corporations Act or CATSI corporation or an incorporated association`)
    AND ((NOT `it`'s `it is a deductible gift recipient`) OR `it`'s `the s 205-35(3A) exception applies`)
    AND (NOT `it`'s `it is in a reporting group`)
    AND `it`'s `the most government grants it received in this or either of the last 2 years` AT MOST 100000
    AND (NOT `it`'s `it is named in a redress application and not a participating institution`)

§§ `s 45-10 -- the governance standards`

-- s 45-10(1): "The regulations may specify standards (the governance standards) with which an entity must comply in order to become
-- registered under this Act, and to remain entitled to be registered under this Act." (2): they may require governing rules to
-- provide for a matter, outcomes (with or without principles), or processes. s 45-5(2) Note 1: "The main consequence of failure to
-- comply with these standards is a loss of the entity's entitlement to registration. If the entity is a federally regulated entity,
-- such a failure to comply may also result in enforcement action under Chapter 4." (5): "The regulations must not require a
-- registered entity to do, or not to do, a thing ... if the registered entity is a basic religious charity." THE STANDARDS ARE IN
-- THE REGULATIONS, NOT DEPOSITED: whether my foundation meets them is an input everywhere it matters (s 25-5(3)(b), s 35-10(1)(c)(ii),
-- s 65-5(2), ss 80-5, 100-5).
@export Can the governance standards apply to my foundation at all (s 45-10(1), (5))?
GIVEN `it is a basic religious charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your foundation is a basic religious charity (s 205-35)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the governance standards bind my foundation` IF
    NOT `it is a basic religious charity`

-- s 45-10(6): "The regulations must not require an entity not to comment on, or advocate support for, a change to any matter
-- established by law, policy or practice in the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or another country, if: (a) the comment or
-- advocacy furthers, or is in aid of, the purpose of the entity; and (b) the comment or advocacy is lawful."
@export Is my foundation's advocacy for a change in law or policy protected from the governance standards (s 45-10(6))?
GIVEN `it furthers my foundation's purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the comment or advocacy furthers, or is in aid of, the foundation's purpose
      `it is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the comment or advocacy is lawful
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation's advocacy protected` IF
    `it furthers my foundation's purpose` AND `it is lawful`

§§ `s 205-25 -- what size is my foundation`

-- s 205-25(1): "A registered entity is a small registered entity for a particular financial year if the revenue of the registered
-- entity for the financial year is less than $250,000, or any other amount prescribed by the regulations". (2): medium if "(a) it
-- is not a small registered entity ...; and (b) the revenue ... is less than $1,000,000, or any other amount prescribed". (3): large
-- if neither. (4): "Revenue is to be calculated ... in accordance with accounting standards". (5): "The Commissioner may continue to
-- treat a registered entity as either a small, medium or large registered entity for a financial year" if it was that size last year
-- and is likely to return to it next year -- the Commissioner's opinion, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Size` IS ONE OF
    `small`
    `medium`
    `large`

@export What size of registered entity is my foundation for the financial year (s 205-25)?
GIVEN `revenue` IS A NUMBER @desc The foundation's revenue for the year, calculated under the accounting standards, in dollars
      `the small threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The small entity threshold: $250,000 in the Act, or another amount prescribed by the Regulations (not deposited)
      `the medium threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The medium entity threshold: $1,000,000 in the Act, or another amount prescribed by the Regulations (not deposited)
      `the Commissioner keeps last year's size` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner continues to treat the foundation as last year's size (s 205-25(5))
      `last year's size` IS A `Size` @desc The foundation's size last financial year (used only if the Commissioner keeps it)
GIVETH A `Size`
`What size is my foundation` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner keeps last year's size` THEN `last year's size`
    ELSE IF `revenue` LESS THAN `the small threshold`
         THEN `small`
         ELSE IF `revenue` LESS THAN `the medium threshold`
              THEN `medium`
              ELSE `large`

§§ `ss 60-5, 60-10, 60-20, 60-25, 60-60 -- what my foundation must lodge`

-- s 60-5(1): "A registered entity must give a statement (an information statement) for a financial year to the Commissioner in the
-- approved form." s 60-10(1): "A medium registered entity or a large registered entity must give the Commissioner a financial report
-- for a financial year, together with any auditor's report or reviewer's report". s 60-20(1): a medium entity must have it
-- "reviewed ... [and] obtain a reviewer's report; or ... audited ... [and] obtain an auditor's report"; (2): the Commissioner "may,
-- by written notice ..., provide that paragraph (1)(a) does not apply" (audit then required). s 60-25: "A large registered entity
-- must: (a) have its financial report ... audited ...; and (b) obtain an auditor's report." s 60-60(1): Subdivision 60-C "does not
-- apply to a basic religious charity" (unless it gives a financial report anyway, (2)).
DECLARE `What my foundation must lodge` IS ONE OF
    `an information statement only`
    `an information statement and a financial report, reviewed or audited`
    `an information statement and an audited financial report`

@export What must my foundation lodge with the Commissioner for the financial year (ss 60-5, 60-10, 60-20, 60-25, 60-60)?
GIVEN `size` IS A `Size` @desc The foundation's size for the year (s 205-25)
      `it is a basic religious charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a basic religious charity (s 205-35)
      `the Commissioner has excluded review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has given written notice that review will not do for a medium entity (s 60-20(2))
GIVETH A `What my foundation must lodge`
`What must my foundation lodge` MEANS
    IF `it is a basic religious charity` THEN `an information statement only`
    ELSE CONSIDER `size`
         WHEN `small` THEN `an information statement only`
         WHEN `medium` THEN IF `the Commissioner has excluded review`
                            THEN `an information statement and an audited financial report`
                            ELSE `an information statement and a financial report, reviewed or audited`
         OTHERWISE `an information statement and an audited financial report`

-- s 60-5(2): "no later than 31 December in the following financial year". s 60-10(2): the same, "or such later time as the
-- Commissioner allows". s 60-85(2)(b): with a substituted accounting period, "the last day of the 6-month period after the end of the
-- accounting period". For a year ending 30 June the two agree (the 6 months after 30 June end on 31 December), so one rule serves
-- both: the day before the date 6 months after the day after the period ends. s 190-15: the Commissioner may defer the time.
@export By when must my foundation lodge its information statement and any financial report (ss 60-5(2), 60-10(2), 60-85(2)(b), 190-15)?
GIVEN `the last day of the year` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the financial year (30 June) or of the approved substituted accounting period, ISO 8601
      `the Commissioner allowed a later day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has deferred the time or allowed a later day
      `the later day` IS A DATE @desc The later day allowed (ignored if none), ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my foundation lodge` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner allowed a later day` THEN `the later day`
    ELSE `add months` (`the last day of the year` PLUS 1) 6 MINUS 1

-- s 60-65(2): after finding "a material error in the statement or report", the entity "must give a corrected statement or report to
-- the Commissioner: (a) if the entity is a small registered entity--within 60 days after the entity identifies the error; or (b) if
-- the entity is a medium registered entity or a large registered entity--within 28 days".
@export By when must my foundation give a corrected statement or report after finding a material error (s 60-65)?
GIVEN `size` IS A `Size` @desc The foundation's size (s 205-25)
      `the day it found the error` IS A DATE @desc The day the foundation identified the material error, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my foundation correct the error` MEANS
    CONSIDER `size`
    WHEN `small` THEN `the day it found the error` PLUS 60
    OTHERWISE `the day it found the error` PLUS 28

§§ `s 55-5 -- records`

-- s 55-5(1): "A registered entity must keep written financial records that: (a) correctly record and explain its transactions and
-- financial position and performance; and (b) enable true and fair financial statements to be prepared and to be audited". (2):
-- "written records that correctly record its operations". (3): in English or readily convertible. (4): "retain the records for 7
-- years after the transactions, operations or acts covered by the records are completed", unless (5) the Commissioner notifies that
-- it need not. (6): "A registered entity commits an offence if the entity does not comply with this section. Penalty: 20 penalty
-- units." (7): strict liability.
@export Until when must my foundation keep the records of a transaction (s 55-5(4))?
GIVEN `the day the transaction was completed` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction, operation or act the records cover was completed, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when must my foundation keep the records` MEANS
    `add years` `the day the transaction was completed` 7

@export Must my foundation still keep the records of a transaction on a given day (s 55-5(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the day the transaction was completed` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction, operation or act the records cover was completed, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, ISO 8601
      `the Commissioner said they need not be kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has notified in writing that these records need not be retained
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my foundation still keep the records` IF
        (NOT `the Commissioner said they need not be kept`)
    AND `the day` AT MOST `Until when must my foundation keep the records` `the day the transaction was completed`

-- s 205-5(3): "The trustee of a trust is taken to be an entity consisting of the person who is the trustee". Crimes Act 1914 s 4B(3):
-- for a body corporate, "a pecuniary penalty not exceeding an amount equal to 5 times the amount of the maximum pecuniary penalty that
-- could be imposed ... on a natural person". INFERENCE: the offence by a trust whose trustee is a company is the trustee company's,
-- so the 5 times applies.
@export What is the most my foundation's trustee can be fined for not keeping or retaining records (s 55-5(6); Crimes Act 1914 s 4B(3))?
GIVEN `the trustee is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee that commits the offence is a company
      `the penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, indexed), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my foundation can be fined for its records` MEANS
    20 TIMES `the penalty unit` TIMES (IF `the trustee is a body corporate` THEN 5 ELSE 1)

§§ `s 65-5 -- the duty to notify`

-- s 65-5(1): "A registered entity must notify the Commissioner in the approved form if any of the following circumstances exist: (a)
-- its name has changed; (b) its address for service has changed; (c) an entity has ceased to be, or has become, a responsible entity
-- of the registered entity; (d) its governing rules have changed; (e) the circumstances described in subsection (2)." (2): it "(i)
-- has contravened a provision of this Act; or (ii) has not complied with a governance standard or external conduct standard; and (b)
-- the contravention or non-compliance is significant ...; and (c) as a result ... the registered entity is no longer entitled to be
-- registered". (3): significance takes account of "the nature, significance and persistence" of it and the proper application of
-- contributions -- the entity's own judgment, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `What has happened` HAS
    `its name changed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its address for service changed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `someone became or ceased to be a responsible entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its governing rules changed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contravened the Act or did not comply with a standard` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contravention or non-compliance is significant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a result it is no longer entitled to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `h` IS A `What has happened` @desc What has happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is significant non-compliance` IF
        `h`'s `it contravened the Act or did not comply with a standard`
    AND `h`'s `the contravention or non-compliance is significant`
    AND `h`'s `as a result it is no longer entitled to be registered`

GIVEN `h` IS A `What has happened` @desc What has happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is an ordinary change` IF
        `h`'s `its name changed`
    OR  `h`'s `its address for service changed`
    OR  `h`'s `someone became or ceased to be a responsible entity`
    OR  `h`'s `its governing rules changed`

@export Must my foundation notify the Commissioner (s 65-5(1), (2))?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What has happened` @desc What has changed or gone wrong
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my foundation notify the Commissioner` IF
    `there is an ordinary change` `what happened` OR `there is significant non-compliance` `what happened`

-- s 65-5(4): "The notification must be given: (a) as soon as practicable; and (b) subject to paragraph (c)--no later than 28 days
-- after the registered entity first becomes aware of the circumstances ...; and (c) if the registered entity is a small registered
-- entity and the notification relates only to circumstances mentioned in paragraph (1)(a), (b), (c) or (d)--no later than 60 days".
-- The outer limit is returned; "as soon as practicable" may be earlier.
@export What is the latest day by which my foundation must notify the Commissioner (s 65-5(4))?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What has happened` @desc What has changed or gone wrong
      `size` IS A `Size` @desc The foundation's size (s 205-25)
      `the day it first became aware` IS A DATE @desc The day the foundation first became aware of the circumstances, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my foundation notify the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF `size` EQUALS `small` AND (NOT `there is significant non-compliance` `what happened`)
    THEN `the day it first became aware` PLUS 60
    ELSE `the day it first became aware` PLUS 28

§§ `ss 80-5, 100-5, 100-10, 100-15 -- can I be warned, suspended or removed`

-- s 80-5(1): a formal warning may be given if "(a) a registered entity is a federally regulated entity and the Commissioner reasonably
-- believes that: (i) the registered entity has contravened a provision of this Act; or (ii) it is more likely than not that [it]
-- will ...; or (b) [it] is a federally regulated entity and the Commissioner reasonably believes that: (i) the registered entity has
-- not complied with a governance standard; or (ii) it is more likely than not that [it] will not ...; or (c) the Commissioner
-- reasonably believes that ... [it] has not complied with an external conduct standard" (or likely will not). s 100-5(1) is the same
-- gate for suspension and removal; (2): it "does not apply to an entity that is a responsible entity ... only because of paragraph
-- 205-30(c)"; (3): not "in relation to a registered entity that is a basic religious charity". s 100-10(1), 100-15(1): the
-- Commissioner may suspend or remove "if the Commissioner considers that doing so is necessary to address the contravention or
-- non-compliance".
DECLARE `The Commissioner's view of my foundation` HAS
    `my foundation is a federally regulated entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner believes it contravened, or will likely contravene, the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner believes it did not, or will likely not, comply with a governance standard` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner believes it did not, or will likely not, comply with an external conduct standard` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `v` IS A `The Commissioner's view of my foundation` @desc The foundation's status and what the Commissioner reasonably believes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Chapter 4 gate is open` IF
        (`v`'s `my foundation is a federally regulated entity`
         AND (`v`'s `the Commissioner believes it contravened, or will likely contravene, the Act`
              OR `v`'s `the Commissioner believes it did not, or will likely not, comply with a governance standard`))
    OR  `v`'s `the Commissioner believes it did not, or will likely not, comply with an external conduct standard`

@export May the Commissioner give my foundation a formal warning (s 80-5)?
GIVEN `view` IS A `The Commissioner's view of my foundation` @desc The foundation's status and what the Commissioner reasonably believes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my foundation be formally warned` IF
    `the Chapter 4 gate is open` `view`

@export May the Commissioner suspend or remove me as a responsible entity of my foundation (ss 100-5, 100-10(1), 100-15(1))?
GIVEN `view` IS A `The Commissioner's view of my foundation` @desc The foundation's status and what the Commissioner reasonably believes
      `it is a basic religious charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the foundation is a basic religious charity (s 205-35)
      `I am responsible only as an insolvency office-holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a responsible entity only because of s 205-30(c)
      `the Commissioner considers it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner considers suspending or removing you necessary to address (or prevent) the contravention or non-compliance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be suspended or removed` IF
        `the Chapter 4 gate is open` `view`
    AND (NOT `it is a basic religious charity`)
    AND (NOT `I am responsible only as an insolvency office-holder`)
    AND `the Commissioner considers it necessary`

§§ `ss 100-20, 100-25, 40-5(2) -- what suspension or removal does to me`

-- s 100-20(1): "A responsible entity suspended under section 100-10 cannot become a responsible entity of the registered entity until
-- the suspension ends." (2): "A responsible entity removed under section 100-15 cannot become a responsible entity of the registered
-- entity." (3): if an individual is a responsible entity because "the registered entity is a company (or is a trust, a trustee of
-- which is a company); and (ii) the individual is a director of the company" and is suspended or removed, "the individual ceases to
-- be a director of the company (until, in the case of suspension, the suspension ends)".
DECLARE `My standing` IS ONE OF
    `neither suspended nor removed`
    `suspended`
    `removed`

@export Do I cease to be a director of my foundation's trustee company (s 100-20(3))?
GIVEN `standing` IS A `My standing` @desc Whether you have been suspended or removed under Division 100
      `I am responsible because I direct the company that is, or is the trustee of, my foundation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a responsible entity because you are a director of the foundation (a company) or of its company trustee
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, ISO 8601
      `the day the suspension ends` IS A DATE @desc The time set in the suspension notice (ignored unless suspended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I cease to be a director` IF
        `I am responsible because I direct the company that is, or is the trustee of, my foundation`
    AND (CONSIDER `standing`
         WHEN `removed` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `suspended` THEN `the day` LESS THAN `the day the suspension ends`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

@export May I become a responsible entity of my foundation again (s 100-20(1), (2))?
GIVEN `standing` IS A `My standing` @desc Whether you have been suspended or removed under Division 100
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, ISO 8601
      `the day the suspension ends` IS A DATE @desc The time set in the suspension notice (ignored unless suspended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I become a responsible entity again` IF
    CONSIDER `standing`
    WHEN `removed` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `suspended` THEN `the day` AT LEAST `the day the suspension ends`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 100-25(1): an offence if the entity "is suspended ... or removed ...; and (b) the entity makes, or participates in making,
-- decisions that affect the whole, or a substantial part, of the business of the registered entity." (2): "exercises the capacity to
-- affect significantly the registered entity's financial standing". (3): an individual who "communicates instructions or wishes to
-- the remaining responsible entities ... (i) knowing that those responsible entities are accustomed to act in accordance with [them];
-- or (ii) intending that [they] will act in accordance with those instructions or wishes", unless it "is advice given ... in the
-- proper performance of functions attaching to the entity's professional capacity or ... business relationship". "Penalty:
-- Imprisonment for 1 year or 50 penalty units, or both."
DECLARE `What I did while suspended or removed` HAS
    `I am suspended or removed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I made or took part in decisions affecting the whole or a substantial part of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I exercised the capacity to affect its financial standing significantly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I passed instructions or wishes to the remaining responsible entities, knowing they act on them or intending they would` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was proper professional or business advice` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Do I commit an offence by still managing my foundation after being suspended or removed (s 100-25)?
GIVEN `conduct` IS A `What I did while suspended or removed` @desc What you did after the suspension or removal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by managing my foundation` IF
        `conduct`'s `I am suspended or removed`
    AND (    `conduct`'s `I made or took part in decisions affecting the whole or a substantial part of its business`
         OR  `conduct`'s `I exercised the capacity to affect its financial standing significantly`
         OR  (    `conduct`'s `I passed instructions or wishes to the remaining responsible entities, knowing they act on them or intending they would`
              AND (NOT `conduct`'s `it was proper professional or business advice`)))

@export What is the most I can be fined for managing my foundation while suspended or removed, besides up to 1 year in prison (s 100-25)?
GIVEN `the penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, indexed), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for managing while suspended` MEANS
    50 TIMES `the penalty unit`

-- s 40-5(1)(f)(v): the Register includes details of "each suspension or removal made under Division 100". (2): "The Commissioner must
-- not include the information mentioned in paragraph (1)(f) before the end of 14 days after the day ... the suspension or removal
-- occurs, unless the Commissioner considers that the public interest requires the information to be included earlier."
@export What is the earliest day my suspension or removal can appear on the Register (s 40-5(2))?
GIVEN `the day it occurred` IS A DATE @desc The day the suspension or removal occurred, ISO 8601
      `the Commissioner considers the public interest requires it earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner considers the public interest requires earlier publication
GIVETH A DATE
`When may my suspension or removal be published` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner considers the public interest requires it earlier` THEN `the day it occurred`
    ELSE `the day it occurred` PLUS 15

§§ `ss 175-35, 175-40 -- a penalty for lodging late`

-- s 175-35: liable if "required under this Act to give a report, return, notice, statement or other document to the Commissioner in
-- the approved form by a particular day; and (b) the entity does not ... by that day." s 175-40(1): "(a) if the entity is a medium
-- registered entity--double the base penalty amount; or (b) if the entity is a large registered entity--5 times the base penalty
-- amount; or (c) otherwise--the base penalty amount." (2): "1 penalty unit for each period of 28 days or part of a period of 28 days
-- ... (up to a maximum of 5 penalty units)." Example: "An entity lodges a return 31 days late. The base penalty amount ... is 2
-- penalty units." (3): the penalty unit at the start of each 28-day period -- one value is used here.
GIVEN `days late` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the due day to the day of lodgement
GIVETH A NUMBER
`periods of 28 days or part` MEANS
    IF TRUNC (`days late` DIVIDED BY 28) 0 TIMES 28 LESS THAN `days late`
    THEN TRUNC (`days late` DIVIDED BY 28) 0 PLUS 1
    ELSE TRUNC (`days late` DIVIDED BY 28) 0

@export What penalty can my foundation be made to pay for lodging late (ss 175-35, 175-40)?
GIVEN `the day it was due` IS A DATE @desc The day the statement, report or notice was due, ISO 8601
      `the day it was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day it was given in the approved form, ISO 8601
      `size` IS A `Size` @desc The foundation's size (s 205-25)
      `the penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, indexed), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What penalty for lodging late` MEANS
    IF `the day it was lodged` AT MOST `the day it was due` THEN 0
    ELSE `units` TIMES `multiplier` TIMES `the penalty unit`
    WHERE
        `periods` MEANS `periods of 28 days or part` (Day `the day it was lodged` MINUS Day `the day it was due`)
        `units` MEANS IF `periods` GREATER THAN 5 THEN 5 ELSE `periods`
        `multiplier` MEANS
            CONSIDER `size`
            WHEN `small` THEN 1
            WHEN `medium` THEN 2
            OTHERWISE 5

§§ `ss 175-10, 175-20, 175-25, 175-30 -- a penalty for a false or misleading statement`

-- s 175-10(1): liable if the entity "makes a statement to the Commissioner ...; and (b) the statement is false or misleading in a
-- material particular". (3): "not liable ... if the entity, and the entity's agent (if relevant), took reasonable care". s 175-20(1)
-- table: "intentional disregard of this Act" -- 60 penalty units; "recklessness ... as to the operation of this Act" -- 40; "a
-- failure ... to take reasonable care to comply with this Act" -- 20; (2): the greatest applies. s 175-25: "Increase the amount by
-- 20% of the base penalty amount if" the entity obstructed the Commissioner, learned of it and did not tell within a reasonable time,
-- or had been liable before. s 175-30(1): "Reduce the amount by 20% of the base penalty amount if" told voluntarily after being told
-- of an examination, saving significant time or resources; (2): "Reduce the amount to nil if the entity voluntarily tells the
-- Commissioner ... before" being told of the examination. (3), the Commissioner treating a later disclosure as earlier, is an input:
-- answer "before".
DECLARE `How the statement came to be wrong` IS ONE OF
    `intentional disregard of the Act`
    `recklessness as to the Act`
    `a failure to take reasonable care`

DECLARE `My foundation's statement` HAS
    `it is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foundation and its agent took reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cause` IS A `How the statement came to be wrong`
    `it obstructed, kept quiet, or was penalised before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it told the Commissioner voluntarily before an examination was notified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it told the Commissioner after an examination was notified, saving significant time` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my foundation liable to a penalty for a false or misleading statement (s 175-10)?
GIVEN `s` IS A `My foundation's statement` @desc The statement and how it came about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation liable for a false statement` IF
    `s`'s `it is false or misleading in a material particular` AND (NOT `s`'s `the foundation and its agent took reasonable care`)

@export What penalty can my foundation be made to pay for a false or misleading statement (ss 175-15 to 175-30)?
GIVEN `s` IS A `My foundation's statement` @desc The statement and how it came about
      `the penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, indexed), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What penalty for a false statement` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Is my foundation liable for a false statement` `s`) THEN 0
    ELSE `base` PLUS `base` TIMES `increase` DIVIDED BY 100 MINUS `base` TIMES `reduction` DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `base` MEANS `the penalty unit` TIMES (CONSIDER `s`'s `the cause`
                                               WHEN `intentional disregard of the Act` THEN 60
                                               WHEN `recklessness as to the Act` THEN 40
                                               OTHERWISE 20)
        `increase` MEANS IF `s`'s `it obstructed, kept quiet, or was penalised before` THEN 20 ELSE 0
        `reduction` MEANS
            IF `s`'s `it told the Commissioner voluntarily before an examination was notified` THEN 100 PLUS `increase`
            ELSE IF `s`'s `it told the Commissioner after an examination was notified, saving significant time`
                 THEN 20
                 ELSE 0

§§ `ss 180-20, 180-25 -- what falls on me as a director of the trustee`

-- s 180-20(1): "an obligation that is imposed under this Act on a trust is imposed on each of the following entities, but may be
-- discharged by any such entity: (a) each entity ... that was a trustee of the trust at the time the obligation arose; (b) if the
-- trustee ... is a company that is a body corporate--each individual who was a director of such a company at the time the
-- obligation arose."
@export Is an obligation the Act imposes on my foundation also imposed on me (s 180-20(1))?
GIVEN `my foundation is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered entity is a trust
      `I was a trustee when it arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a trustee when the obligation arose
      `I was a director of a company trustee when it arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a director of a body corporate trustee when the obligation arose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation's obligation also mine` IF
    `my foundation is a trust` AND (`I was a trustee when it arose` OR `I was a director of a company trustee when it arose`)

-- s 180-20(2): "An amount that is payable under this Act by a trust is payable by ... (a) each entity ... that was a trustee ... at
-- the time the amount became payable; (b) if the trustee ... is a company that is a body corporate--each individual who was a
-- director of such a company at the time the amount became payable." (3): "An amount is payable by a director under paragraph (2)(b)
-- only if the amount is payable by the trust because of a deliberate act or omission of the director involving dishonesty, gross
-- negligence or recklessness." (4): jointly and severally liable. s 180-35: a director who pays has a guarantor's rights against the
-- others.
DECLARE `My part in an amount my foundation owes` HAS
    `my foundation is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was a trustee when it became payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was a director of a company trustee when it became payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is owed because of my deliberate act or omission involving dishonesty, gross negligence or recklessness` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I personally liable to pay an amount my foundation owes under the Act (s 180-20(2), (3))?
GIVEN `p` IS A `My part in an amount my foundation owes` @desc Your position when the amount became payable, and your part in it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I personally liable for my foundation's amount` IF
        `p`'s `my foundation is a trust`
    AND (    `p`'s `I was a trustee when it became payable`
         OR  (    `p`'s `I was a director of a company trustee when it became payable`
              AND `p`'s `it is owed because of my deliberate act or omission involving dishonesty, gross negligence or recklessness`))

-- s 180-25: "An offence against this Act committed by a trust no trustee of which is a body corporate is taken to have been committed
-- by each entity that was a trustee of the trust at the time the trust committed the offence." Nothing in Subdivision 180-C makes the
-- directors of a company trustee commit the trust's offence.
@export Is an offence committed by my foundation taken to be committed by me (s 180-25)?
GIVEN `a trustee of my foundation is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any trustee of the foundation is a company
      `I was a trustee when the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were yourself a trustee when the offence was committed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foundation's offence mine` IF
    (NOT `a trustee of my foundation is a body corporate`) AND `I was a trustee when the offence was committed`
